  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On rue du Lys, opposite the square des Frères Gaudino Joly, the city of Cannes opened this 400 m² dog park on 23 December 2024. It is fully fenced (1.20 m fence) with two entrances, and has a meadow, a stabilised area, an agility course (walkway and seesaw), a fountain for dogs and their owners, a hose to clean them, two waste-bag dispensers, bins and three benches.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The park is open every day from 8:30am to 6:30pm (source: city of Cannes). Dogs must stay under their owner's supervision and have up-to-date vaccinations, and category 1 and 2 dogs are not allowed. Remember to pick up waste.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: still fairly little known, it's a good option for a relaxing break without too many people outside weekends.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Central Cannes and the Croisette are a few minutes away on foot or by car.</p>
